    {
      "id": "873ebb25-21a4-4621-97a6-2541ef3a4d4a",
      "name": "Sticky Note c2e0e69d",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Automation 02: Invoice Reminders\n\n### Introduction\nEvery weekday at 9am, this workflow finds overdue invoices, sends staged payment reminders and gives finance a daily summary. No AI is used.\n\n### What to key in\nIn the **Receivables** tab of the Google Sheet, add one row per invoice:\ninvoice_no, client_name, client_email, issue_date, due_date (yyyy-mm-dd), amount_sgd, paid_sgd, status (Unpaid, Part Paid, Paid, Cancelled, Disputed or On Hold), reminder_count (start at 0).\nLeave last_reminded blank.\n\n### What happens next\n1. Only Unpaid and Part Paid invoices are checked.\n2. Reminders go out 1, 7 and 14 days overdue, showing the amount still owing and PayNow details.\n3. The reminder count and date are saved in the row.\n4. After the third reminder, the invoice is listed for finance to call.\n5. Bad dates, missing emails and unknown statuses go to the **Exceptions** tab.\n6. **Email Finance Summary** is always sent, even with 0 overdue.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect your Gmail account in **Send Reminder** and **Email Finance Summary**.\n2. In **Config**, enter finance_email, company_name and paynow_uen.\n3. Test with test_mode on, which sends every email to test_email.\n4. For live use, set test_mode to false and publish.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 760
      }
    }
